  "result": "Fixed: completion arguments containing `#` are now kept intact.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment. Everything after a `#` was dropped, so `cli a#b` was parsed as `cli a`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is treated as an ordinary character.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b` and a leading `#a`. They pass along with the existing parser and shell-completion tests (67 passed).\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry.",
